hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6291","I asked Anas b. Malik: How was the hair of Messenger of Allah ﷺ? Thereupon he said: His hair was neither very curly nor very straight, and they hung over his shoulders and earlobes. (Using translation from Muslim 2338a)"
"6292","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): Did the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) have white hair? He replied: Allah Almighty did not make him appear old through white hair. There were not more than 17 or 18 white hairs in his blessed head and beard."
"6293","I counted only fourteen (14) white hairs in the head and beard of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"6294","“The white hair of the Prophet ﷺ numbered approximately twenty.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3630)"
"6295","I have seen approximately twenty white hairs of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), which were at the front."
"6296","The Messenger of Allah [SAW] did not dye his hair; his gray hair were only a little beneath his lower lip and at his temples, and a little on his head. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5087)"
"6297","His face was as (bright) as the sword. Thereupon he (Jabir) said: No, it was round and like the sun and the moon. And I saw the seal near his shoulder of the size of a pigeon's egg and its color was the same as that of his body. (Using translation from Muslim 2344b)"
"6298","The narrator says: It was like the egg of a pigeon."
"6299","narrates: He visited the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) and also saw the Seal of Prophethood between his two shoulders."
"6300","I removed the cloth from the blessed back of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), then I took the Seal of Prophethood between my two fingers and pressed it lightly. He was asked: What was that seal? He replied: It was some hair that was gathered at one place near his shoulder."
"6301","I saw the Seal of Prophethood between the two shoulders of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, which was like a pigeon’s egg. Its color was like the color of the blessed body of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him."
"6302","The Seal of Prophethood was present on the back of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), which was like a lump (similar to a fruit of the jujube tree). On it was written: ""Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah."
"6303","I have never touched any silk or brocade that was softer than the blessed palm of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), and I have never smelled any fragrance or sweat that was more fragrant than the sweat of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him)."
"6304","I have never smelled any musk or amber more pure than the fragrance of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him)."
"6305","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more modest than a veiled virgin girl."
"6306","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more modest than a veiled virgin girl."
"6307","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) this statement: ""The Prophet (peace be upon him) was more modest than a veiled virgin girl. When something displeased him, we could perceive it on his face."
"6308","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was more modest than a virgin in her chamber. If he disliked something, that could be seen in his face.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4180)"
"6309","""I have not seen anything more beautiful than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. It was as if the sun flowed upon his face. And I have not seen anyone quicker in his walking than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. It was as if the earth was made easy for him. We would be exerting ourselves while he would not be struggling."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3648)"
"6310","The complexion of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was radiant, and his sweat was like pearls. When he walked, he walked briskly and leaned forward slightly."
"6311","I have not seen anyone like him before or after him."
"6312","""When the Prophet walked, his Companions would walk in front of him, and he would leave his back for the angels."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 246)"
"6313","I have many names: I am Muhammad, I am Ahmad, I am al-Mahi through whom Allah obliterates unbelief, and I am Hashir (the gatherer) at whose feet people will be gathered, and I am 'Aqib (after whom there would be none), and Allah has named him as compassionate and merciful. (Using translation from Muslim 2354b)"
"6314","I am Muhammad, Ahmad. Muqaffi (the last in succession), Hashir, the Prophet of repentance, and the Prophet of Mercy. (Using translation from Muslim 2355)"
"6315","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saying this in a street of Madinah Munawwarah: ""I am Muhammad, I am Ahmad, I am Hashir, Muqaffi, and the Prophet of Mercy."
"6316","‘He used to elongate his voice.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1353)"
"6317","The recitation of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was drawn out. He (peace be upon him) would recite ""Bismillah"" in a drawn-out manner. He would recite the word ""Ar-Rahman"" in a drawn-out manner. He would recite the word ""Ar-Raheem"" in a drawn-out manner."
"6318","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) reciting (the Qur’an). I have not heard anything more beautiful than the recitation of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"6319","The statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), ""I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, 'Last night I recited before the jinn,'"" is a clear indication that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) was not present that night. If he had been present that night, he would not have narrated this incident from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as a report, that he recited before the jinn, but rather he would have informed that he himself was present at that time when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited before the jinn."
"6320","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ‘A representative of the jinn came to me, so I went with them and recited (the Qur’an) before them.’ (The narrator says) Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went with us and showed us the traces of those jinn and their fire.”"
"6321","I heard Abu Ubaidah saying: I heard Masruq saying, your father narrated this hadith to me: ""On the night of meeting with the jinn, a tree tried to frighten the Prophet (peace be upon him) through the jinn."
"6322","The Prophet ﷺ read the Qur'anic verse, ""And take ye the Station of Abraham as a place of prayer. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3969)"
"6323","The narrator says: When I reached that verse, I took the page on which I was writing the Qur’an and presented it to Sayyidah Hafsah, may Allah be pleased with her. She said: Write it like this: “Guard your prayers, and especially the middle prayer, which is the Asr prayer, and stand before Allah with humility.”"
"6324","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When a believer testifies in the grave that there is no deity except Allah and recognizes Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), then this is what is meant by Allah Almighty's statement: 'Allah will keep the believers firm with the firm word in the life of this world and in the Hereafter.'"
"6325","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""If you wish, you can attain reward for it."" That is, the word in it was recited with lightness."
"6326","I ask you about anything after this, then do not remain with me."" In this, it is with the word of hamzah: ""You have received an excuse from me."
"6327","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to recite this: « » ."
"6328","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) stating this. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) recited « » that is, he recited it with ""dal""."
"6329","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made me read the verse ""It is I who give (all) sustenance, Lord of power, steadfast (for ever). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3993)"
"6330","The narrator says: We replied: All of us can. He asked: Who among you has the most knowledge of recitation? The narrator says: My companions pointed towards me. Sayyiduna Abu Darda’ asked: Do you remember? I replied: Yes. He asked: How did Sayyiduna Abdullah recite Surah Al-Lail? I said: He used to recite it like this: « » He said: Do you remember these words from the tongue of Sayyiduna Abdullah? I replied: Yes. He said: By the One besides whom there is no deity! I also learned these words in the same way from the tongue of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), but these people want me to recite with (other words). By Allah! I will never accept what they say."
"6331","I said: « » . Sayyiduna Abu Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with him) said: These people have constantly caused me to doubt about this, although I myself heard this verse (in this way) from the tongue of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"6332","I saw the Prophet ﷺ reading the verse; ""does he think that his wealth would make him last for ever?"" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3995)"
"6333","that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Indeed, Allah chose Kinanah from the children of Isma'il, and He chose Quraish from Kinanah, and He chose Hashim from Quraish, and He chose me from Banu Hashim."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3606)"
"6334","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Jibreel (peace be upon him) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). At that time, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was playing with children. (That is, this incident took place during the childhood of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him.) He caught the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), laid him down, split open his chest, took out a clot of blood from it and"
"6335","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was in my lap, and during that time, Allah Almighty produced so much milk in my breast that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) drank from it and drank to his fill. His foster brother also drank from it, meaning Sayyidah Halimah's son also drank from it, until he too was satisfied. At night, my husband went to our she-camel, and its udder was also full of milk. My husband milked as much as we wanted. He drank and was satisfied, and I"
"6336","I saw the mark of that incision on the blessed chest of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"6337","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Do you consider or see that my face is towards the Qibla? By Allah, neither your submissiveness nor your bowing is hidden from me, surely I see you from my back."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 418)"
"6338","I see behind me just as I see in front of me. You people should straighten your rows and perform bowing and prostration properly."
"6339","The Prophet ﷺ said: Stand close together in your rows, bring them near one another, and stand neck to neck, for by Him in Whose hand my soul is, I see the devil coming in through openings in the row just like a small black sheep. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 667)"
"6340","I have seen the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that even light types of dates were not available to him in such quantity that he could fill his stomach with them."
"6341","narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was hungry, even such light types of dates were not available to him in sufficient quantity that he could fill his stomach."
"6342","I heard Nu'man deliver an address in which he said that (Hadrat) Umar made a mention of what had fallen to the lot of people out of the material world and he said: I saw Messenger of Allah ﷺ spend the whole day being upset because of hunger and he could not get even an interior quality of dates with which he could fill his belly. (Using translation from Muslim 2978)"
"6343","“O Allah, make the provision of the family of Muhammad sufficient for them.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4139)"
"6344","“O Allah, make the provision of the family of Muhammad sufficient for them.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4139)"
"6345","The family of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) never ate to their fill for three consecutive days, until the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away. Their food consisted of only two black things, dates and water."
"6346","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) never fed his family with wheat bread to their fill for three consecutive days, until he departed from this world."
"6347","I asked Sahl bin Saʿd, ""Did Messenger of Allah ﷺ ever eat white flour?"" Sahl said, ""Messenger of Allah ﷺ never saw white flour since Allah sent him as an Apostle till He took him unto Him."" I asked, ""Did the people have (use) sieves during the lifetime of Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" Sahl said, ""Messenger of Allah ﷺ never saw (used) a sieve since Allah sent him as an Apostle until He took him unto Him,"" I said, ""How could you eat barley unsifted?"" he said, ""We used to grind it and then blow off its husk, and after the husk flew away, we used to prepare the dough (bake) and eat it."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 5413)"
"6348","Son of my sister, by Allah, I used to see the new moon, then the new moon, then the new moon, i. e. three moons in two months, and fire was not kindled in the house of Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I ('Urwa) said: Auntie, then what were your means of sustenance? She said: Dates and water. But it (so happened) that Messenger of Allah ﷺ had some Ansar as his neighbours and they had milch animals and they used to send to Messenger of Allah ﷺ some milk of their (animals) and he served that to us. (Using translation from Muslim 2972c)"
"6349","The narrator says: At that time, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) had nine wives."
"6350","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose Hand is the life of Muhammad, if I had gold equal to the mountai"
"6351","Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him). I said: O Bilal, tell me how t"
"6352","Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). At that time,"
"6353","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came to the house of Lady Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her). He saw a curtain han"
"6354","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would not enter a house in which there were pictures or engravings."
"6355","“We used to go to (visit) Anas bin Malik.” (One of the narrators) Ishaq said: “And his baker was standing there.” (In another narration) Darimi said: “And his table was set. He said one day: ‘(Come and) eat, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ never saw any thin loaf of bread until he met Allah, nor any roasted sheep (with skin).’”* (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3339)"
"6356","""The Prophet ﷺ would not store anything for the morrow."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2362)"
"6357","The wealth of Banu an-­Nadeer was among the fai' that Allah bestowed upon His Messenger ﷺ, for which the Muslims made no expedition with either cavalry or camelry (cf. al-Hashr 59:6). It was only for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he used to spend from it on his family's annual expenses-and on one occasion he said: his annual food supply ­-and what was left he spent on horses and weapons in preparation for jihad for the sake of Allah, may He be glorified and exalted, (Using translation from Aḥmad 171)"
"6358","Messenger of Allah ﷺ died (in a state) that it never happened that he could eat to his fill the bread with olive oil twice during a day. (Using translation from Muslim 2974)"
"6359","narrates: Bread and meat were never combined together on the dining mat of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for the morning and evening meals, except in the case when he was eating with other people."
"6360","I asked Sahl bin Saʿd, ""Did Messenger of Allah ﷺ ever eat white flour?"" Sahl said, ""Messenger of Allah ﷺ never saw white flour since Allah sent him as an Apostle till He took him unto Him."" I asked, ""Did the people have (use) sieves during the lifetime of Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" Sahl said, ""Messenger of Allah ﷺ never saw (used) a sieve since Allah sent him as an Apostle until He took him unto Him,"" I said, ""How could you eat barley unsifted?"" he said, ""We used to grind it and then blow off its husk, and after the husk flew away, we used to prepare the dough (bake) and eat it."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 5413)"
"6361","The bed of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) was made of leather and filled with palm leaves. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Sometimes a month would pass over us in such a way that we could not light a fire (for cooking) throughout the month. Our food consisted of only two black things, dates and water. However, sometimes our neighbors would send us milk from their goats."
"6362","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was resting on a bed made of date-palm fiber rope. The narrator states: During this time, some of his companions came to him, and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) also entered. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) turned to his side, the marks of the rope were visible on his side. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) began to weep and said: By Allah! We know that you are more honored in the sight of Allah than Kisra and Caesar, yet both of them are living lives of luxury. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Are you not pleased that these things are for them in this world and for us in the Hereafter? Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Yes. The narrator says: Then he remained silent."
"6363",": “The Messenger of Allah said: ‘I have been sent with concise speech and I have been supported with fear. While I was sleeping, the keys to the treasures of the Earth were brought to me and placed in my hands.’” Abu Hurairah said: “The Messenger of Allah has gone and you are acquiring them.” (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3087)"
"6364","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""The keys of the world were brought to me, loaded on a piebald horse, upon which there was a sheet made of silk.\"""""
"6365","Sayyiduna Jibreel (peace be upon him) was sitting with the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). During this, he looked towards the"
"6366","(Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) There is a possibility that initially it was forbidden for the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) to marry more women than a specified number, and then before his passing, it was made lawful for him to marry women (without any specified number). This was a special favor bestowed upon him (peace be upon him). In this case, there will remain no contradiction or difference between the hadith and the Book of Allah, and this is indicated by Lady Aisha’s (may Allah be pleased with her) acceptance that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) did not pass away until it was made lawful for him to marry women (without any specified number). So, by this, Lady Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) means: this was a permission that came after a previous prohibition, as we have mentioned earlier."
"6367","Lady Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I used to get very angry at those women who would offer themselves in marriage to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). I used to think, could any woman offer herself for marriage? When Allah the Exalted revealed this verse:"
"6368","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) about the inheritance of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), so Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Are you asking me about the inheritance of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)? May your father perish! By Allah, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) did not leave behind in inheritance any dinar or dirham or slave or slave-girl or goat or camel."
"6369","“He was the best of people, the most generous of people, the most courageous of people. The people of Al-Madinah became alarmed one night, and he was the first of them to investigate the noise and din. He was riding a horse belonging to Abu Talhah, bareback, with no saddle. His sword was hanging from his neck and he was saying: ‘O people, do not be afraid,’ sending them back to their houses. Then he said of the horse, ‘We found it like a sea,’ or, ‘It is a sea.’”* (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2772)"
"6370","""The Messenger of Allah was the most generous of people, and he was most generous in Ramadan when Jibril met him. Jibril use to meet him every night during the month of Ramadan and study Quran with him."" And he said: ""When Jibril met him, the Messenger of Allah was more generous in doing good than the blowing wind."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2095)"
"6371","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) never ate to his fill twice in one day until his passing."
"6372","The narrator asked: O Mother of the Believers! What would the Prophet (peace be upon him) eat then? Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) replied: We had some Ansari neighbors. May Allah reward them with goodness. They had milk, and they would send it as a gift to the Prophet (peace be upon him)."
"6373","narrates: A man came to the service of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), and he (the Prophet) gave him sheep that were between two mountains. That man went to his people and said: O my people! Accept Islam, by Allah! Muhammad (peace be upon him) gives so much to a person that he no longer fears poverty. (Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates:) Sometimes a person would come to the service of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) (to accept Islam). His only purpose was to gain worldly benefit, but then it would happen that his religion would become more beloved to him than the world and all that is in it."
"6374","The Prophet (peace be upon him) ordered that he be given all the goats present between two mountains. He returned to his people and said: Accept Islam, for Muhammad (peace be upon him) gives so much to a person that he no longer fears poverty."
"6375","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) turned towards him, smiled, and said: Give him something!"
"6376","narrates: Whenever anything was asked from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), he never refused."
"6377","narrates: Whenever anything was asked from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he never said ""no."
"6378","""The Prophet ﷺ would not store anything for the morrow."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2362)"
"6379","Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-Aas (may Allah be pleased with him) addressed the people in a sermon and said: ""O people! Your Prophet was the most disinterested in the world, and now you are the most desirous of the world."
"6380","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) has gone nearby; he was at the house of a tailor who was his freed slave. He had prepared food for him, which included pumpkin and meat. The narrator says: I noticed that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) liked pumpkin, so I started placing it before him. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) returned to his home, so I placed that vessel before him. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) kept eating from it and also kept distributing it, until nothing was left in that vessel."
"6381","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to accept gifts, but he would not accept charity."
"6382","narrates: When food from someone else's house was brought to the service of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), he would inquire about it. If it was said that it was a gift, the Prophet (peace be upon him) would eat it with us, and if it was said that it was charity, the Prophet (peace be upon him) would say: ""You people eat it,"" and the Prophet (peace be upon him) himself would not eat it."
"6383","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""I have decided that from now on I will not accept any gift, except from a person who is a Qurayshi, an Ansari, a Thaqafi, or a Dosi.\"""""
"6384","The Prophet (peace be upon him) gave him something in return and asked: ""Ar"
"6385","I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! Are you going to sleep without performing Witr?"" I asked this question to express the importance of Witr, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""O Aisha! My eyes sleep but my heart does not sleep."
"6386","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""My eyes sleep, but my heart does not sleep."
"6387","Anas b. Malik reported that Messenger of Allah ﷺ was neither very conspicuously tall nor short-statured, and his color was neither glaringly white nor brown; his hair was neither very curly nor very straight; Allah commissioned him (as a Prophet) when he had reached the age of forty years, and he stayed in Mecca for ten years and for ten years in Medina; Allah took him away when he had just reached the age of sixty, and there had not been twenty white hair in his head and beard. (Using translation from Muslim 2347a)"
"6388","narrates: When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away, he was 63 years old."
"6389","Anas b. Malik reported that Messenger of Allah ﷺ died when he was sixty-three years old, and so was the case with Abu Bakr, and so was the case with Umar who was also sixty-three (when he died). (Using translation from Muslim 2348)"
"6390","narrates: When the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) was sent as a Prophet, he was 40 years old. He (peace be upon him) invited people to Islam, but for thirteen years he was not permitted to fight. Then, after the migration, there were ten years, then the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) passed away, and at that time he (peace be upon him) was 63 years old."
"6391","""The ring of the Messenger of Allah [SAW] was of silver and its stone (Fass) was made of silver too."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5198)"
"6392","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to write a letter to the non-Arab (rulers), so people informed him: They only read a letter that has a seal with an inscription on it. So, under the command of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), a silver ring was made. On it was inscribed: ""Muhammad, Messenger of Allah."
"6393","""The inscription on the ring of the Prophet ﷺ was in three lines: 'Muhammad' on a line, 'Messenger' on a line, and 'Allah' on a line."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1747)"
"6394","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wore a silver ring with an Ethiopian gemstone, and he used to ear the stone in towards his palm. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3646)"
"6395","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) wore a black cloak, so Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! How beautiful this looks on you. Your fair complexion stands out with its blackness, and its blackness stands out with your fair complexion. Then you perceived an odor from that cloak, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) took it off. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) liked pure fragrance."
"6396","We asked Anas b. Malik: Which cloth was dearer to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ? or Which cloth did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ like best to wear ? He replied: The striped cloaks (hibrah). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4060)"
"6397","I have also seen Qasim and Salim doing the same."
"6398","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “I have been given five things which were not given to anyone before me. I have b"
"6399","Sayyiduna Awf bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""Four things have been granted to me which were not granted to anyone before us. I asked my Lord for a fifth thing, and He granted that to me as well. Previously, a prophet would be sent specifically to his own community, and he would not go beyond that community, but I have been sent to all of mankind. Our enemy is struck with awe from a distance of a month's journey."
"6400","The entire earth has been made a place of prayer for us, and its soil has been made a means of purification for us when we do not find water. Our rows (in prayer) have been made like the rows of angels. And I have been given the last verses of Surah Al-Baqarah from the treasure beneath the Throne; such verses have not been given to anyone before me nor will they be given to anyone after me."
"6401","""I have been honored over the Prophets with six (things): I have been given Jawami' Al-Kalam, I have been aided by (the ability to cause in the enemy) fright, the spoils of war have been made lawful for me, the Earth has been made as a Masjid and purifier for me, and I have been sent to all creatures, and with me Prophethood is sealed."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1553)"
"6403","""I have been honored over the Prophets with six (things): I have been given Jawami' Al-Kalam, I have been aided by (the ability to cause in the enemy) fright, the spoils of war have been made lawful for me, the Earth has been made as a Masjid and purifier for me, and I have been sent to all creatures, and with me Prophethood is sealed."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1553)"
"6404","Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Sulayman informed us in Fustat, al-Harith ibn Miskin narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih informed me from Sa'id ibn Suwayd from Abd al-A'la ibn Hilal al-Sulami from al-Irbad ibn Sariyah al-Fazari (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Indeed, I am written with Allah as the Seal of the Prophets, while Adam was still kneaded in his clay, and I will inform you of the beginning of that: the supplication of my father Abraham, the good tidings of Jesus, and the dream of my mother when she gave birth to me that there came out of her a light which illuminated for her the palaces of Syria."""
"6405","The similitude of mine and that of the Apostles before me is that of a person who built a house quite imposing and beautiful, but for one brick in one of its corners. People would go round it, appreciating the building, but saying: Why has the brick not been fixed here? He said: I am that brick and I am the last of the Apostles. (Using translation from Muslim 2286c)"
